ins required before final sign-off, since the currently committed DoorPrototype.unity on disk still reflects the pre-repair UI configuration.\\\",\\\"criteria_results\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R1-ProgressUI-ConfiguredByBuilder\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs BuildUI() creates a 'ProgressFill' background Image and a nested 'Fill' child Image, assigning UI/Skin/UISprite.psd as the sprite with type=Filled, fillMethod=Horizontal, fillOrigin=Left. This directly fixes the diagnosed root cause (a Filled Image with sprite==null always renders full/solid regardless of fillAmount). New Edit Mode test Build_ProgressFillImage_HasSpriteAssignedSoFillAmountIsVisible in Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs asserts sprite non-null, type Filled, fillMethod Horizontal after Build().\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R2-UI-ReceivesProgressContinuously\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Scripts/DoorInteractionUI.cs Update() runs progressFillImage.fillAmount = door.Progress every frame, unconditionally while progressFillImage is assigned; DoorInteractable.Tick (called from its own Update) mutates Progress every frame during an active interaction, so with a real sprite now assigned the fill will visibly animate continuously.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R3-Reset-OnRelease-Movement-Damage\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"DoorInteractable.CancelInteraction() sets Progress = 0f. PlayerInteractionController.EndInteraction() (called from EndInteraction on release, OnPlayerMoved, and HandleDamaged on PlayerHealth.Damaged) invokes CurrentDoor.CancelInteraction(). DoorInteractionUI.Update() re-reads \"\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n      \"role\": \"Door and Interaction Agent — Controls HUD Enhancement\",\r\n      \"prompt\": \"AgentCrew/prompts/02_implementer.md\",\r\n      \"started_at_utc\": \"2026-08-05T00:25:11.708675+00:00\",\r\n      \"finished_at_utc\": \"2026-08-05T00:28:43.127754+00