session_id\": \"63f2e512-4565-406d-8e1e-1b6b5f4d4938\",\r\n      \"num_turns\": 31,\r\n      \"result_excerpt\": \"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Static review of the Controls HUD scope amendment and the prior progress-indicator repair finds no blocking code, contract, test, reference, or compilation problems. Labels are hardcoded to match the current default key bindings (E, K, WASD), the HUD is rebuilt fresh every run alongside the rest of Canvas with dedicated idempotency tests, it is a sibling object positioned to avoid the prompt/progress bar, the progress-fill sprite regression fix is intact and covered by an Edit Mode test, no runtime script touches UnityEditor, and no excluded systems or external packages were introduced. Human Play Mode verification of visual layout is still required and cannot be substituted by this review.\\\",\\\"criteria_results\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"HUD-1: scene builder creates a readable controls panel every time it runs\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:269 calls BuildControlsHud(canvasObject.transform) at the end of every BuildUI() call, and Canvas is in KnownRootNames (line 27) so it is destroyed and rebuilt from scratch on every Build(). Covered by Build_ControlsHud_ExistsSeparateFromPromptAndProgressIndicator in DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs:44-55.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"HUD-2: displayed labels match the actual input implementation\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"PlayerInteractionController.cs:9 defaults interactKey=Key.E, DebugDamageControl.cs:11 defaults damageKey=Key.K, PlayerMovement.cs:28-31 reads WASD — all match the hardcoded HUD text 'WASD - Move / Hold E - Open Door / ... K - Take Damage' in DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:305-309. Build_ControlsHud_TextMatchesActualImplementedControls (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs:58-76) asserts the actual serialized damageKey value's ToString() appears in the HUD text.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"HUD-3: panel includes WASD movement, Hold E to open, and interruption rule\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:305-309 text literal contains all three; asserted by StringAssert.Contains checks at DoorPrototypeSc\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"human_repair_status\": \"validation_passed\",\r\n  \"human_repair_started_at_utc\": \"2026-08-05T00:15:18.281422+00:00\",\r\n  \"human_playtest_feedback_file\": \"AgentCrew/inputs/human_playtest_feedback.md\",\r\n  \"human_repair_finished_at_utc\": \"2026-08-05T00:20:22.590294+00:00\",\r\n  \"targeted_ui_status\": \"validation_passed\",\r\n  \"targeted_ui_started_at_utc\": \"2026-08-05T00:25:11.699812+00:00\",\r\n  \"targeted_ui_scope_amendment\": \"AgentCrew/inputs/approved_scope_amendment_controls_hud.md\",\r\n  \"targeted_ui_finished_at_utc\": \"2026-08-05T00:30:55.372485+00:00\"\r\n}\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
